WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.770
A parent asked our teacher: how did

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.390
the class do in the maths test?

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.890
We had nine marks in front

4
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.290
of us, without names.

5
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.820
Nobody wants to hear all nine.

6
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.750
We needed one fair number.

7
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.520
Today: three kinds of middle, and

8
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.420
how to measure the spread.

9
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:22.010
The mean is what everyone would get

10
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.830
if we shared the total equally.

11
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.930
Add all the marks, then divide

12
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.190
by how many there are.

13
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.100
Our nine marks add to one hundred and

14
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.600
sixteen, so the mean is about thirteen.

15
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.100
The median is the middle mark when

16
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.280
you line them up in order.

17
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.900
With nine marks, it is the fifth one.

18
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.580
Here, the median is thirteen.

19
00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.470
The mode is the mark that

20
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.670
appears most often.

21
00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.890
Here, twelve and fourteen both appear

22
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.090
twice, so there are two modes.

23
00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.800
The mode is handy for things you

24
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.280
cannot add, like favourite colours.

25
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:01.990
Now watch.

26
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.240
One pupil was ill and scored zero.

27
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.240
The mean drops to about eleven.

28
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.200
The median only moves to twelve.

29
00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:14.050
One extreme mark pulls the mean,

30
00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.050
but hardly moves the median.

31
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.390
A middle alone is not enough.

32
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.140
Two classes can have the same mean, but

33
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.420
one has marks from nine to sixteen, and

34
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.340
the other from two to twenty.

35
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.720
The range, highest minus

36
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.500
lowest, shows the spread.

37
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.340
Quick check!

38
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.060
Most pupils get a little pocket

39
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.600
money, but one gets a lot.

40
00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.300
Which middle describes a

41
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.620
typical pupil best?

42
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:45.380
The median.

43
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.480
The one big amount pulls the mean up, so

44
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.560
the mean looks richer than most pupils

45
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:51.880
are.

46
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.300
The median stays with the typical pupil.

47
00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.230
In the app, open The

48
00:01:58.230 --> 00:01:59.430
middle and the spread.

49
00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.540
Drag one pupil's mark from zero to

50
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.340
twenty, and watch the mean,

51
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.840
median, mode and range react.

52
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:08.730
Your turn.

53
00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.020
A class has a range of eighteen marks.

54
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.580
What does that tell you about the class?

55
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.820
The marks are very spread out.

56
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.930
Remember: the mean shares out,

57
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.830
the median is the middle, the

58
00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.710
mode is the most common.

59
00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.920
And always give a spread with your middle.

60
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.960
Try it yourself: ask ten friends how

61
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:34.200
many minutes they walk to school.

62
00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.050
Work out the mean, the median

63
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.170
and the range, and say which

64
00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.890
middle describes them best.
